    {
      "id": "0zd35JfsTWw12V7F9uBJO",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1736.6950175762177,
      "y": -286.96639347076416,
      "width": 809.8992919921875,
      "height": 675,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0q",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 742236367,
      "version": 1492,
      "versionNonce": 582268175,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1773328589944,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "We never force company's to onboard. We expose fraud apis to them.\n\nClaimants registered\n\nWe expose an API which the insurance companies \ncan directly use, with the Blockchain Fraud Network \naccess.\n\nIf they choose to use our platform for the claiming and everything\nWe can directly handle everything on platform itself\n - The fraud detection\n - Blockchain based verification\n - Twilio based Whatsapp Integration for a better accessibility, and experience\n - Twilio based Outbound calls to the hospitals and the garages for a simple QnA\n   as a part of verification validation\n - Ofcourse we will have our own set of validations, if hospital claims are false,\n   the hospitals are corrupt and risk scoring becomes higher on the company side\n - AI for the OCR, Geographic analysis, environment check, morphed images, staged\n   accidents, etc etc.\n - Agents for chats, specialized subagents for specialised tasks in the complete\n   workflow.\n - And Vedant ne jo bhi chize batayi hai voh sab.\n\nUSP :\n- Blockchain ka fraud network we are sharing with the help of apis.\n- Twilio based call and whatsapp integrations for verifications and instant claims.\n- Aur batao.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "We never force company's to onboard. We expose fraud apis to them.\n\nClaimants registered\n\nWe expose an API which the insurance companies \ncan directly use, with the Blockchain Fraud Network \naccess.\n\nIf they choose to use our platform for the claiming and everything\nWe can directly handle everything on platform itself\n - The fraud detection\n - Blockchain based verification\n - Twilio based Whatsapp Integration for a better accessibility, and experience\n - Twilio based Outbound calls to the hospitals and the garages for a simple QnA\n   as a part of verification validation\n - Ofcourse we will have our own set of validations, if hospital claims are false,\n   the hospitals are corrupt and risk scoring becomes higher on the company side\n - AI for the OCR, Geographic analysis, environment check, morphed images, staged\n   accidents, etc etc.\n - Agents for chats, specialized subagents for specialised tasks in the complete\n   workflow.\n - And Vedant ne jo bhi chize batayi hai voh sab.\n\nUSP :\n- Blockchain ka fraud network we are sharing with the help of apis.\n- Twilio based call and whatsapp integrations for verifications and instant claims.\n- Aur batao.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "93t73x60VOOZ6D20TYWbd",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2672.1950175762177,
      "y": -306.46639347076416,
      "width": 511.1595153808594,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0r",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 525743503,
      "version": 439,
      "versionNonce": 825488513,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1773328776320,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The set of insurance claim sectors we can look at : \n1. Health care mediclaims\n2. Automobile accident related claims.\n3. Property Insurance.\n4. Life insurance. (Disabled)\n5. Travel insurance. (Disabled)\n\nWe will actively be working on the first 3.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The set of insurance claim sectors we can look at : \n1. Health care mediclaims\n2. Automobile accident related claims.\n3. Property Insurance.\n4. Life insurance. (Disabled)\n5. Travel insurance. (Disabled)\n\nWe will actively be working on the first 3.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wsmA7-bKtmykN68hnLjl-",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2673.1950175762177,
      "y": -84.96639347076416,
      "width": 604.439453125,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0s",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1858620975,
      "version": 247,
      "versionNonce": 1252244577,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1773328776320,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "We will need to find all the validation, verification approaches,\napis, models, to detect frauds\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "We will need to find all the validation, verification approaches,\napis, models, to detect frauds\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ETI1FyfZUeaiY3RL35yJG",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2677.2567989826202,
      "y": -4.96639347076416,
      "width": 596.6389160156249,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0t",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 561831873,
      "version": 421,
      "versionNonce": 1207069807,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1773328932713,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Normal google based searching would also help find the\nhospitals or other garages which will be used for the\nverifications ofc",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Normal google based searching would also help find the hospitals or other garages which will be used for the verifications ofc",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "FHW-PBJHizdq5THB5Mg4p",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2723.3283711346708,
      "y": 184.4404669674961,
      "width": 1482.918701171875,
      "height": 575,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0u",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1408166369,
      "version": 2071,
      "versionNonce": 1339797729,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1773332653256,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Primary Features : \n \n- Company : \n     - Company can check their Policy holders, have access rights.\n     - Company can verify the claims if they need a HITL.\n     - Chat interface to chat globally across the system or specific to the policy holder.\n\n - Claimants : \n                                      WEB INTERFACE\n\n     - Document Upload (ID proofs [one time]), OCR, Image reading. \n     - Forms and Chat (Agent) The prompts will be type wise categorized.\n     - Image Pipeline -> Damage Estimation\n     - Textual Data -> Plus Damage Estimation se we will do -> Policy verifications\n     - Knowledge graph (Generic) -> Verification as per the Policy rules which are defined | Active Policy.\n     - Fraud Detection -> ML model, Anomaly detection system, Plus Tamper detections\n     - Validate Duplicate Claims with the Blockchain based fraud detection network.\n     - When it is all clear we need a payout pipeline. (If the accuracy is high, we can schedule the payment in short duration)\n     - If it is risk free then if the amount claimed is less than 10k we directly schedule, but if greater than ofc we need a HITL. \n       RISK HAI to fir HITL. 70% and above -> instant payout, below 70% -> HITL (Manual verification) [Company k interface yahan pe chat daaldena]\n     - Blockchain : Documents will be stored on blockchain, Transactions jo hue hai, insurance company uske actions, approve reject krta\n                                      WHATSAPP INTERFACE\n      -  ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Primary Features : \n \n- Company : \n     - Company can check their Policy holders, have access rights.\n     - Company can verify the claims if they need a HITL.\n     - Chat interface to chat globally across the system or specific to the policy holder.\n\n - Claimants : \n                                      WEB INTERFACE\n\n     - Document Upload (ID proofs [one time]), OCR, Image reading. \n     - Forms and Chat (Agent) The prompts will be type wise categorized.\n     - Image Pipeline -> Damage Estimation\n     - Textual Data -> Plus Damage Estimation se we will do -> Policy verifications\n     - Knowledge graph (Generic) -> Verification as per the Policy rules which are defined | Active Policy.\n     - Fraud Detection -> ML model, Anomaly detection system, Plus Tamper detections\n     - Validate Duplicate Claims with the Blockchain based fraud detection network.\n     - When it is all clear we need a payout pipeline. (If the accuracy is high, we can schedule the payment in short duration)\n     - If it is risk free then if the amount claimed is less than 10k we directly schedule, but if greater than ofc we need a HITL. \n       RISK HAI to fir HITL. 70% and above -> instant payout, below 70% -> HITL (Manual verification) [Company k interface yahan pe chat daaldena]\n     - Blockchain : Documents will be stored on blockchain, Transactions jo hue hai, insurance company uske actions, approve reject krta\n                                      WHATSAPP INTERFACE\n      -  ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "AsLJpI1LFSEUNGP2WkRdJ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4320.583511222492,
      "y": -69.68686684695149,
      "width": 396.0396728515624,
      "height": 2350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0v",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 12921519,
      "version": 104,
      "versionNonce": 1932371489,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1773338939014,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A. Healthcare Claims (Mediclaim)\nRequired Documents\nhospital bill\n\ndischarge summary\n\nprescription\n\ndiagnostic reports\n\npolicy document\n\nID proof\n\nFraud Signals\nCheck for:\n\nDuplicate medical bills\n\nAbnormally high treatment costs\n\nSuspicious hospital patterns\n\nSame patient claiming multiple policies\n\nFake discharge summaries\n\nmismatched treatment codes\n\nreused medical reports\n\nB. Automobile Insurance\nRequired Documents\naccident photos\n\nrepair invoice\n\ngarage estimate\n\nvehicle RC\n\ndriver license\n\ninsurance policy\n\nFIR (if severe accident)\n\nFraud Signals\nCheck for:\n\nReused accident images\n\ninflated repair estimates\n\nstaged accidents\n\ngarage fraud rings\n\nduplicate claims across insurers\n\ninconsistent accident location/time\n\nrepeated claims from same vehicle\n\nC. Property Insurance\nRequired Documents\nproperty ownership proof\n\ndamage photos\n\nrepair estimate\n\nincident report\n\ninsurance policy\n\nID proof\n\nFraud Signals\nCheck for:\n\nreused damage images\n\nclaiming pre‑existing damage\n\nexaggerated repair estimates\n\nsuspicious contractor networks\n\nmultiple claims on same property\n\naltered documents\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A. Healthcare Claims (Mediclaim)\nRequired Documents\nhospital bill\n\ndischarge summary\n\nprescription\n\ndiagnostic reports\n\npolicy document\n\nID proof\n\nFraud Signals\nCheck for:\n\nDuplicate medical bills\n\nAbnormally high treatment costs\n\nSuspicious hospital patterns\n\nSame patient claiming multiple policies\n\nFake discharge summaries\n\nmismatched treatment codes\n\nreused medical reports\n\nB. Automobile Insurance\nRequired Documents\naccident photos\n\nrepair invoice\n\ngarage estimate\n\nvehicle RC\n\ndriver license\n\ninsurance policy\n\nFIR (if severe accident)\n\nFraud Signals\nCheck for:\n\nReused accident images\n\ninflated repair estimates\n\nstaged accidents\n\ngarage fraud rings\n\nduplicate claims across insurers\n\ninconsistent accident location/time\n\nrepeated claims from same vehicle\n\nC. Property Insurance\nRequired Documents\nproperty ownership proof\n\ndamage photos\n\nrepair estimate\n\nincident report\n\ninsurance policy\n\nID proof\n\nFraud Signals\nCheck for:\n\nreused damage images\n\nclaiming pre‑existing damage\n\nexaggerated repair estimates\n\nsuspicious contractor networks\n\nmultiple claims on same property\n\naltered documents\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
